  "tagline": "Transparent persistence for Python objects with ACID transactions and history.",
  "description": "ZODB is a native object database for Python. You subclass Persistent, attach objects to a root mapping, and they are saved transparently at transaction commit, with no ORM or schema involved. It provides ACID transactions with optimistic concurrency and conflict resolution, scalable BTrees for large collections, history and undo in FileStorage, and multi-client access through ZEO or RelStorage. It has backed Zope and Plone for over two decades, and the Zope Foundation still ships regular releases (6.4 in October 2026). It fits Python apps with deep object graphs better than tabular data or non-Python consumers.",
